      "question": "What things do they look for in a home inspection?",
      "answer": "An inspector examines the primary structural components and operating systems throughout the property. This review includes the roof covering, foundation walls, surface drainage, electrical panels, plumbing fixtures, heating units, cooling equipment, attic insulation, and interior living areas. The tool lists these items for your home and flags findings that are red flags."
