      "question": "What's the worst thing a home inspector can find?",
      "answer": "The most serious findings are structural problems, active water intrusion and safety hazards. The tool's red flags are horizontal or wide foundation cracks, active roof leaks and soil sloping toward the house. Old knob-and-tube wiring and aluminum branch wiring also matter."
